            <ArticleTitle>Periarticular heterotopic ossification after multiple knee ligament reconstructions. A report of three cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>398-401</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Heterotopic ossification is a frequently encountered clinical and radiographic entity. There are no previous reports in the English literature of heterotopic ossification after arthroscopically assisted ligament reconstructions for knee dislocations. Further, a link between the PCL reconstruction and posterior capsular ossification has not been heretofore recognized. Our three cases should raise the clinical awareness of such an entity.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
